    "notes": "Profile of Irek Kusmierczyk, Liberal MP for Windsor-Tecumseh (2019-2025). Born January 16, 1978 in Krasnik, Poland; came to Canada as a political refugee in 1983. PhD in Political Science from Vanderbilt University. Served as Windsor City Councillor for Ward 7 (2014-2019) before entering federal politics. Parliamentary Secretary to the Minister of Employment, Workforce Development and Disability Inclusion. Lost his seat in 2025 by just 4 votes to Conservative Kathy Borrelli after a judicial recount. Wikidata Q62940707.",
